Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:17:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] tests: process-level 3-owner fixture (real nats-server +
 mycelic process + SDK)

Three owners in separate teams each hold one fragment (transport, buffer,
demand) of a supply risk on sd-9; distractors are an unrelated entity, a
similarly named entity, a resent root, a denied owner in another enterprise
with a canary string, and noise. Asserts abstention, exact roots, cross-org
404s, broker+service restart, retraction withdrawing the conclusion and
rebuild from JetStream. A missing broker fails the test instead of skipping.

Committed as reviewed. The adversarial review found that several assertions
pass for the wrong reason (abstention is vacuous: the query is not
entity-bound and no other entity is completed; the sd-90 check cannot fire;
wait_idle ignores ack-pending). Those findings are recorded in
research/mycelic/ingestion_tesseract_20261024 and are not fixed by editing
this test.

